# Bestie Check

Before returning a document deliverable, prepare it with Check and read its Quick Look.

Use the single `bestie-check` MCP server. This plugin configures it over stdio (`npx -y @mybestie/check mcp`). Hosts that connect by URL (connectors in Claude, ChatGPT, Grok, Muse) use https://www.hirebestie.com/api/check/mcp **instead**; never configure both. Do not reimplement Check.

## Sequence

1. `inspect_capabilities` once.
2. `prepare_deliverable` (text or URL) or `prepare_file_upload` → PUT → `confirm_file_upload` (files). Keep the `uploadHandleId`; never paste file bytes.
3. Poll `get_preparation` while `nextAction` is `wait`. On `retry`, call `retry_preparation` once. On `replace_source`, prepare the source again once.
4. On `review`, report the claims and assumptions as returned. Never grade them.

Paid verification (`quote_check`, `verify_deliverable`, `create_repair`) exists only when `inspect_capabilities` reports `paidExecution.available: true`. When it does not, do not call those tools, do not promise the user a verdict, a price or findings, and say that paid verification is not open (give the reason `inspect_capabilities` returned). When it does, it runs only against a quote the user approved. You never approve spend on the user's behalf. Paid runs need the user's explicit, quote-bound approval (the quote id, its hash and a server-verified approval reference (`--approval-ref`) and credit ceiling: `--approve-quote`, `--approve-quote-hash`, `--approve-up-to`); rules and plugins never grant it.

